WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
Have a plan for you and your family before

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.540
severe weather happens. Have an emergency kit ready and

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.940
know where you will go for shelter.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.240
When you know high winds are in the area,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.900
bring loose items and pets inside and secure trash

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.580
cans. Here are some alerts you may receive and

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.740
the differences between them.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.540
A tornado watch means all the ingredients of severe

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.620
weather are present in the area and are coming

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.160
together. A tornado warning means severe weather is imminent

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.260
or occurring and you should seek shelter.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.500
Remain sheltered in place until the tornado threat has

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.180
passed. Remember to duck.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.580
Go down to the lowest level of your home,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.240
get under something sturdy at the center of your

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.060
house, and keep away from your windows.
